---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="About | Bryce Mason">
  <section class="page">
    <div class="about-grid">
      <div class="card about-text">
        <p class="mini-label">About</p>
        <h1>Background, interests, and direction.</h1>

        <p>
          I grew up in Marin County, just north of San Francisco. Growing up,
          Mt. Tam and abundant nature were all around me. I was outside
          constantly, and that is where my interest in the environment actually
          started.
        </p>

        <p>
          At Whitman College in Walla Walla, WA, that interest became more
          analytical. I graduated cum laude in May 2026 with a BA in
          Economics-Environmental Studies and a minor in Finance, which gave me
          a way to think carefully about how markets and the environment fit
          together. Outside of class, I was involved with the Whitman Investment
          Company, including the Finance Accelerator and the Investment Banking
          Competition, which pushed me to sharpen my thinking on valuation, deal
          structure, and how to present an idea under pressure. A liberal arts
          education also taught me to move across disciplines and get up to speed
          quickly, which has carried into my work in finance, strategy, and
          business decision-making.
        </p>

        <p>
          Professionally, I am now an Associate Finance Analyst at G3 Enterprises
          in Modesto, CA. Prior to that, I worked on finance and sales operations
          at G3 as an intern, finance and feasibility analysis with Perca, and
          M&amp;A research at Unsal Partners. Across those roles, I have been
          drawn to work that mixes structured thinking with real business problems,
          especially in industries where the analysis is still being figured out.
        </p>

        <p>
          Going forward, I want to keep doing finance and strategy work that
          stays close to real business problems and where careful analysis
          actually drives decisions. I am especially drawn to investing and to
          industries like climate that are still being figured out, but my
          interests are broad across finance and finance-adjacent work. Over
          time, I want to grow into an analyst and investor whose work is
          practical and tied to the industries shaping the next few decades.
        </p>

        <p>
          Outside of work, I spend as much time outdoors as the season allows —
          skiing, hiking, and anything else I can find. I also try to keep
          learning from people doing interesting things in investing and climate.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="photo-stack">
        <div class="card photo-card">
          <img src="/linkedinphoto.jpg" alt="Bryce Mason" />
        </div>

        <div class="card photo-card">
          <img src="/fun-photo.jpg" alt="Bryce Mason hiking" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page {
    max-width: 1100px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .about-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.45fr) 280px;
    gap: 24px;
    align-items: start;
  }

  .card {
    background: #1c1f22;
    border: 1px solid #2a2e33;
    border-radius: 28px;
    padding: 28px;
  }

  .mini-label {
    font-size: 0.84rem;
    color: #a9c2af;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4rem);
    margin-bottom: 24px;
    line-height: 1.02;
  }

  p {
    color: #d0d4d8;
    font-size: 1.06rem;
    line-height: 1.9;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .photo-stack {
    display: grid;
    gap: 18px;
  }

  .photo-card {
    padding: 18px;
  }

  .photo-card img {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 240px;
    display: block;
    margin: 0 auto;
    border-radius: 20px;
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .about-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .photo-stack {
      max-width: 360px;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .card {
      padding: 24px;
      border-radius: 24px;
    }
  }
</style>